# Known dtbs_check complaints that are expected, with the reason each one is here.
#
# These are nodes we carry only to satisfy MediaTek's LK, which walks the device tree looking for
# downstream node names and asserts when it does not find them. They describe a bootloader's
# expectations rather than hardware, mainline has no schema for them, and they must be removed before
# anything is submitted upstream. Everything NOT listed here still fails the job.
#
# One regex per line; blank lines and comments ignored.

# LK looks this node up by literal path and writes "okay" into its status property.
reserve-memory-sspm_share: failed to match any schema
# LK finds the SCP node by the vendor compatible "mediatek,scp"; mainline's binding allows one compatible.
scp@10500000 .*compatible.*is too long
/soc/scp@10500000: failed to match any schema with compatible: \['mediatek,mt8183-scp', 'mediatek,scp'\]

# The Cosmo's panel. Otto Pflueger added the panel-simple entry but never upstreamed a binding, so the
# compatible has no schema. Needs a dt-bindings patch before submission -- this is a real gap, not just a
# bootloader accommodation like the entries above.
panel@0: failed to match any schema with compatible: \['planet,cosmocom-x800-datong-panel'\]
